# Pin LF for anything a shell interprets, regardless of platform or core.autocrlf.
#
# Without this, a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true rewrites every shell script in
# the working tree to CRLF. That breaks two things:
#   1. deploy-hooks.js --check hashes the (CRLF) working-tree file against the installed
#      (LF) copy and reports permanent drift, byte-identical or not.
#   2. `#!/bin/bash\r` is a real runtime failure on the self-hosted Linux runner: the
#      kernel looks for an interpreter literally named `bash\r`.
# See #323.
*.sh text eol=lf
hooks/** text eol=lf
